I would say logically infra-red goggles would grant infravision, like 
dwarves get. They can see any non-coldblooded creatures in the dark. I 
think the thick insulating stone walls of the dungeon would prevent you 
being able to see anything not in line of sight (maybe allows through 
doors, but that's all). Regular sources of blindness would not affect 
you (all light is filtered, anyway). In addition, exploding items and 
fire traps (when triggered) should cause blindness with them on.

Still, it doesn't seem like these are terribly useful. Maybe by 
(a)pplying them you can toggle blindness (turn off the goggles), which 
would eliminate the current huge drawback of lenses that you have to 
take them off before putting on a towel.

